Bundled third-party software
----------------------------

This package bundles its own copies of Qt 6 and other third-party libraries
under /opt/plotjuggler4/lib so that it runs independently of the Qt version
installed on the system.

/opt/plotjuggler4/share/doc/plotjuggler4/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt names every
third-party component built into PlotJuggler or shipped with it (Qt and the
code Qt contains, ICU, FFmpeg, the Conan dependency set and the libraries
compiled into those, the Qt Advanced Docking System, Qwt), with its licence and
its copyright and licence text, the GNU GPL and LGPL texts among them; the
About box shows the same file. The copyright files of the bundled distribution
libraries are under /opt/plotjuggler4/share/doc/<package>/, and
DISTRIBUTION-PACKAGES.txt beside THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt records each one's
exact version.

LGPL components. Qt 6 (LGPL-3) and FFmpeg (built LGPL-only, LGPL-2.1 or later)
are shared libraries under /opt/plotjuggler4/lib: replace them with compatible
builds of your own to run PlotJuggler with a modified version. The Qt Advanced
Docking System is PlotJuggler's fork, modified (LGPL-2.1 or later,
https://github.com/PlotJuggler/Qt-Advanced-Docking-System, at the commit the
3rdparty/Qt-Advanced-Docking submodule pins); it, Qwt (LGPL-2.1 with the Qwt
exception), elfutils' libdw (LGPL-3 or later) and libxcrypt (LGPL-2.1 or later,
in the embedded Python) are linked statically. PlotJuggler's complete source at
the release tag, with the pinned dependencies (versions.env, conanfile.txt,
conan.lock) and the build commands (build.sh, docs/BUILDING.md), lets you
rebuild it against a modified copy of any of them.

Corresponding sources: each component's source at the exact version shipped
is available from the locations THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and the PlotJuggler 4
repository name, and on written request via
https://github.com/PlotJuggler/PlotJuggler/issues, for three years after the
release, at no more than the cost of physically performing the distribution.
The request also covers the distribution packages in DISTRIBUTION-PACKAGES.txt.

Bundled plugins under /opt/plotjuggler4/lib/plotjuggler/plugins are published
separately by the PlotJuggler project and carry their own license metadata in
each plugin's manifest.json.

Retro render helper (/opt/plotjuggler4/bin/3rdparty/retro)
-----------------------------------------------------------

pj-raster-helper is an independent executable that PlotJuggler launches as a
child process and links no part of. It is licensed under the GNU General Public
License, version 2 (/usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-2), whose full text also
ships next to the binary as COPYING. Its complete corresponding source —
raster/helper/ in the PlotJuggler 4 repository plus the doomgeneric submodule
pinned there — is covered by the written offer in SOURCE-OFFER.txt, shipped in
the same directory.

base.wad is id Software's unmodified DOOM1.WAD shareware data, redistributed
under the terms in SHAREWARE-LICENSE.txt, shipped in the same directory. It is
data, not a program: no part of PlotJuggler or of the helper is derived from
it.
